    'Leave blank to match the homepage' => 'Leave blank to match the homepage',
    'Excluded URI Patterns' => 'Excluded URI Patterns',
    'Pages whose URI matches one of these regular expressions are excluded from every scan (PHP, browser pass, and overlay). Example: <code>^checkout</code>, <code>print$</code>, <code>^admin/</code>.' => 'Pages whose URI matches one of these regular expressions are excluded from every scan (PHP, browser pass, and overlay). Example: <code>^checkout</code>, <code>print$</code>, <code>^admin/</code>.',
    'Add a URI pattern' => 'Add a URI pattern',
    'Excluded Volumes' => 'Excluded Volumes',
    'Tick any volume whose images you don\'t want in the alt-text audit: avatars, generated thumbnails, system files, anything that isn\'t public content needing alt text. Their images are left out of the Assets page, its counts, and the Asset alt text panel on the dashboard.' => 'Tick any volume whose images you don\'t want in the alt-text audit: avatars, generated thumbnails, system files, anything that isn\'t public content needing alt text. Their images are left out of the Assets page, its counts, and the Asset alt text panel on the dashboard.',
    'No asset volumes exist yet.' => 'No asset volumes exist yet.',
    'Scanned Element Types' => 'Scanned Element Types',
    'Tick the element types the content scanner should cover. Native Craft types (entries, categories) and first-party ones like Commerce products are on by default; a third-party plugin\'s custom element stays off until you tick it here. Unticking a type drops its stored pages and issues from every report.' => 'Tick the element types the content scanner should cover. Native Craft types (entries, categories) and first-party ones like Commerce products are on by default; a third-party plugin\'s custom element stays off until you tick it here. Unticking a type drops its stored pages and issues from every report.',
    'Accessibility Statement' => 'Accessibility Statement',
    'Path to a site template that **replaces** the built-in statement markup, e.g. `_statement/render`. It receives the same `statement` variable and should output the statement itself. This is not the page you publish the statement on: a template that calls `craft.a11y.accessibilityStatementHtml()` would render itself forever, so that is ignored. Leave empty to use the built-in markup.' => 'Path to a site template that **replaces** the built-in statement markup, e.g. `_statement/render`. It receives the same `statement` variable and should output the statement itself. This is not the page you publish the statement on: a template that calls `craft.a11y.accessibilityStatementHtml()` would render itself forever, so that is ignored. Leave empty to use the built-in markup.',
