    'A new overlay token was generated. Copy it now, it won\'t be shown in full again.' => 'A new overlay token was generated. Copy it now, it won\'t be shown in full again.',
    'Decoupled Frontends' => 'Decoupled Frontends',
    'Run the admin overlay on a headless frontend (Next, Nuxt, Astro) with a single script tag. Available on the Pro edition.' => 'Run the admin overlay on a headless frontend (Next, Nuxt, Astro) with a single script tag. Available on the Pro edition.',
    'If your site\'s frontend is not served by Craft, add {tag} to its pages and the overlay runs there too: same axe engine, same rules, results stored against the same scans. Head or footer makes no difference as long as {defer} stays on the tag. The script does nothing for regular visitors. In Craft templates (a hybrid install), use {variable} instead: it resolves this install\'s URL itself and renders nothing when the feature is off.' => 'If your site\'s frontend is not served by Craft, add {tag} to its pages and the overlay runs there too: same axe engine, same rules, results stored against the same scans. Head or footer makes no difference as long as {defer} stays on the tag. The script does nothing for regular visitors. In Craft templates (a hybrid install), use {variable} instead: it resolves this install\'s URL itself and renders nothing when the feature is off.',
    'To activate the overlay in a browser, open the frontend through an activation link: the frontend\'s own URL with {fragment} appended, using the token below. It must be the frontend\'s domain, not this install\'s, because the browser stores the token per domain. A small notice in the corner confirms the activation took. The overlay endpoints only answer requests carrying that token.' => 'To activate the overlay in a browser, open the frontend through an activation link: the frontend\'s own URL with {fragment} appended, using the token below. It must be the frontend\'s domain, not this install\'s, because the browser stores the token per domain. A small notice in the corner confirms the activation took. The overlay endpoints only answer requests carrying that token.',
    'Enable Decoupled Overlay' => 'Enable Decoupled Overlay',
    'Serve the overlay loader and answer its token-authenticated API calls. Independent of the Frontend Overlay toggle under General, which only controls injection on Craft-rendered pages.' => 'Serve the overlay loader and answer its token-authenticated API calls. Independent of the Frontend Overlay toggle under General, which only controls injection on Craft-rendered pages.',
    'Additional Allowed Origins' => 'Additional Allowed Origins',
    'Origins allowed to call the overlay endpoints, one per line, e.g. {example}. Every site\'s base URL origin is always allowed; add entries here for dev servers and preview deployments Craft doesn\'t know about.' => 'Origins allowed to call the overlay endpoints, one per line, e.g. {example}. Every site\'s base URL origin is always allowed; add entries here for dev servers and preview deployments Craft doesn\'t know about.',
    'New overlay token' => 'New overlay token',
    'Current overlay token' => 'Current overlay token',
    'Excluded Elements (CSS selectors)' => 'Excluded Elements (CSS selectors)',
    'Elements matching these selectors are skipped by every scan surface: the PHP scan, the browser pass, the Inspect preview, and the overlay. One selector per line, e.g. {example}. The common consent-management banners (OneTrust, Cookiebot, Ketch and the rest) are always excluded; add anything else on the page you do not control, such as a chat widget.' => 'Elements matching these selectors are skipped by every scan surface: the PHP scan, the browser pass, the Inspect preview, and the overlay. One selector per line, e.g. {example}. The common consent-management banners (OneTrust, Cookiebot, Ketch and the rest) are always excluded; add anything else on the page you do not control, such as a chat widget.',
    'Accessibility statement' => 'Accessibility statement',
    'Answer these {n} separately' => 'Answer these {n} separately',
    'Browser Settle Time (ms)' => 'Browser Settle Time (ms)',
    'How long each browser pass waits after the page loads before running the checks, in milliseconds, so late-rendering JavaScript can finish. The wait is paid on every pass (twice per page, desktop and mobile), so on a large site it is one of the biggest levers on total scan time. Plenty of sites are fine at 500. Set 0 to skip the wait entirely; raise it if client-rendered content is being missed.' => 'How long each browser pass waits after the page loads before running the checks, in milliseconds, so late-rendering JavaScript can finish. The wait is paid on every pass (twice per page, desktop and mobile), so on a large site it is one of the biggest levers on total scan time. Plenty of sites are fine at 500. Set 0 to skip the wait entirely; raise it if client-rendered content is being missed.',
